Q: Are there any nice ways to split Crypto++ Integer in Two? A: <p><a href="https://github.com/weidai11/cryptopp/blob/master/integer.h" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>CryptoCPP::Integer</code></a> supports <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation" rel="nofollow noreferrer">bitwise operations</a>, similarly to built in integral types (<code>int</code> etc.).</p>
<p>Therefore you can do the following:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>rMask(&quot;0x00000000000000000000000000000000ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff&quot;);
xL(x &gt;&gt; 128);
xR(x &amp; rMask);
</code></pre>
